[216.527, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[216.687, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 RUNNING OPENCODE CONTAINERIZED ARD E2E TEST SUITE\r\n================================================================================\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[219.187, "o", "Here's what I found for both topics:\r\n\r\n**SQL Query Optimization:**\r\n- **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines** (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 partitioning/clustering, window functions, schema design: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/skills/main/skills/bigquery/SKILL.md\r\n- **Cloud SQL, AlloyDB & Spanner Database Design** (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 normalization, connection pooling, index design: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/skills/main/skills/databases/SKILL.md\r\n- **BigQuery MCP Server** (tier 3, needs GCP ADC) \u2014 run dry-runs/cost estimates against your real data\r\n\r\n**Zero-Trust Security:**\r\n- **Well-Architected Security** (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 zero-trust patterns, IAM least privilege, network perimeters, encryption: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/skills/main/skills/security/SKILL.md\r\n- **GCP Auth & ADC Playbook** (tier 0, no auth) \u2014 Workload Identity, service account impersonation\r\n- **GKE Networking Skill** (tier 0) \u2014 network policy hardening for zero-trust segments\r\n\r\nBest picks are the two **tier 0 skills** \u2014 usable immediately with no GCP account. Want me to read the full SKILL.md contents for the SQL optimization and zero-trust security guidelines?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization best practices and database performance tuning\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero-trust security architecture tools and best practices for cloud databases\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[219.187, "o", "\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[221.687, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe best fit is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it executes SQL directly on BigQuery tables, supports query dry-run/cost estimation, and handles 100GB+ datasets via BigQuery's serverless engine.\r\n\r\nIt's Tier 3 (needs GCP credentials), with a free tier of 1TB query processing/month. Alternatives: the **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill** (free, offline) for query optimization patterns.\r\n\r\nWant me to onboard BigQuery so we can run the query? You'd run `gcloud auth application-default login` on your terminal.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run live analytical SQL query on BigQuery sales dataset\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[224.187, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nSet your GCP discovery to `opt_out`. I'll skip GCP-required tools unless you ask about them again.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[224.187, "o", "\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Human OAuth & Live BigQuery Query\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[226.687, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe best tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 it can run SQL, inspect schemas, and explore public datasets. It requires GCP credentials (Tier 3). Let me check your\r\n**BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) \u2014 runs SQL, inspects schemas, explores public datasets. Best match.\r\n\r\nAlternatives:\r\n- `bigquery-guidelines` skill (Tier 0, no auth) \u2014 SQL/perf guidance only, can't run queries.\r\n- BigQuery has a free tier (1TB queries/month).\r\n\r\nYour gcloud is installed but not authenticated. Do you want me to onboard you to BigQuery so you can run queries? If yes, I'll record your consent and you'll need to run `gcloud auth application-default login` in your terminal.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query a public BigQuery dataset\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[229.187, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nLogged. Run this on your terminal to authenticate:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen optionally verify with:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth list\r\n```\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:gcloud\",\"decision\":\"onboarded\"}\r\n\r\n--- Turn 3 (Human OAuth Flow) ---\r\n"]
[230.929, "o", "Go to the following link in your browser, and complete the sign-in prompts:\r\n\r\n    https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?response_type=code&client_id=[REDACTED_CLIENT_ID]...&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fsdk.cloud.google.com%2Fapplicationdefaultauthcode.html&scope=openid+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fuserinfo.email+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fcloud-platform&state=[REDACTED]&prompt=consent&access_type=offline\r\n\r\nEnter verification code: 4/0AXEQxID[REDACTED_OAUTH_CODE]\r\n\r\nCredentials saved to file: [/workspace/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json]\r\n\r\nThese credentials will be used by any library that requests Application Default Credentials (ADC).\r\nQuota project \"alanblount-sandbox\" was added to ADC which can be used by Google client libraries for billing and quota.\r\n\r\n"]
[233.429, "o", "--- Turn 4 (Post-Auth Live Query Response) ---\r\nI'll help you query BigQuery public data. Let me first check the auth status and find the\r\nThe BigQuery MCP server that can run this query requires GCP Application Default Credentials, which aren't currently active on this machine (verified: `gcp_authenticated: false`).\r\n\r\nTo run the query against `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`, you'll need to authenticate once. Do you want to proceed with GCP auth so I can execute the query?\r\n\r\nIf yes, run this on your terminal, then tell me:\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\n(Free tier covers this \u2014 1TB/month of free query processing.)\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run SQL query against Google BigQuery public datasets\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 3 Passed: Complete Onboarding & Live BigQuery query executed successfully.\r\n\r\n"]
[233.43, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea PATH A: API Key Only (Tier 1 Gemini Developer API)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[235.93, "o", "The **Gemini API Structured Outputs & Tool Calling Skill** (`urn:ai:google.com:skills:gemini-api-patterns`) is the best match:\r\n\r\n- Covers code generation, multimodal reasoning, function calling, and structured outputs against the Gemini Developer API\r\n- Auth: **API key** (Tier 1) \u2014 no GCP account needed, ready to use now\r\n- Also has context caching and JSON schema constrained decoding patterns\r\n\r\nSecondary option: **Google Developer Knowledge MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:developer-knowledge`) for documentation/lookup help while working with the API.\r\n\r\nWant me to persist your consent to use the Gemini API skill?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"generate code with Gemini Developer API using API key\",\"tier\":1}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Path A Passed: Tier 1 Gemini API tools unlocked without GCP login.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea PATH B: Enterprise Service Account Mount (Tier 3 Automated)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[238.43, "o", "The best fit is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** \u2014 it executes SQL queries, inspects table schemas, and dry-runs queries with cost estimates. It requires GCP credentials (Tier 3). Let me check your auth\r\nTo query enterprise BigQuery, use the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (SQL execution, schema inspection, query cost estimation). However, your GCP auth is currently unauthenticated \u2014 you'll need to run `gcloud auth application-default login`.\r\n\r\nDo you agree to onboard this GCP-tier service?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query enterprise BigQuery dataset SQL\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n\u2705 Path B Passed: Service Account automatically enabled cloud tools.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea PATH C: Changing Mind (Opt-Out -> Opt-In)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[240.93, "o", "Your consent is recorded. Run this in your terminal to finish logging in:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you also want the CLI account configured:\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth login\r\n```\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:gcp\",\"decision\":\"onboarded\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"decision\":\"onboarded\",\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:gcp\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Path C Passed: Stored preferences updated smoothly from opt-out to opt-in.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea TEST 7: Complete ARD & OpenCode Unit and Scenario Suite\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[242.197, "o", "test_canonical_urn_format (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_canonical_urn_format)\r\nVerify all entries in ai-catalog.json strictly use canonical urn:ai: FQDN format. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_1_service_account_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_1_service_account_active)\r\nScenario 1: System has GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS pointing to a valid SA key. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_2_user_adc_active (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_2_user_adc_active)\r\nScenario 2: System has standard application_default_credentials.json. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_3_gcloud_installed_unauthenticated)\r\nScenario 3: gcloud is in PATH, but no credentials are saved. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_4_bare_system_no_gcloud)\r\nScenario 4: Bare system without gcloud or GCP credentials (offline/clean). ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_5_user_opt_out_mode)\r\nScenario 5: User preference set to 'opt_out' -> Tier >= 3 tools are completely excluded. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_6_fallback_skills_and_api_keys)\r\nScenario 6: Verify API key detection (Gemini) and fallback skill links. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences (test_ard_resolver.TestARDResolverAuthScenarios.test_scenario_7_multi_runtime_preferences)\r\nScenario 7: Preferences work in ADK / ephemeral runtimes via env vars & memory. ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_a_opt_out_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_a_opt_out_flow)\r\nScenario A: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_b_gcloud_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario B: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_c_service_account_onboarding_flow)\r\nScenario C: ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_d_gemini_api_key_only (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_d_gemini_api_key_only)\r\nScenario D (Path A): ... ok\r\ntest_scenario_e_change_mind_opt_out_to_opt_in (test_opencode_scenarios.TestOpenCodeDiscoveryScenarios.test_scenario_e_change_mind_opt_out_to_opt_in)\r\nScenario E (Path C): ... ok\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nRan 13 tests in 0.049s\r\n\r\nOK\r\n\r\n\u2705 Test 7 Passed: All 13 unit and scenario tests executed successfully.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83c\udf89 ALL 7 E2E CONTAINER TESTS PASSED!\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
